mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course teaches the basic theories and experimental techniques of medical immunology. The basic immunology section includes: innate immunity and adaptive immunity, specifically, antigens that induce immune responses, immune molecules and immune cells involved in the immune resposes , as well as the immune response process. The clinical immunology section focuses on the immunological mechanisms underlying clinically relevant diseases.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
